@clawsweeper re-review

Head: `351ebf33586e59f2bf0d3216afc2c8e06d43f41a`. Conflict integration retains main's async read owner and carries the PostgreSQL snapshot fields. All 24 PG owner tests, 17 SQLite read-lifecycle tests, core types, Kysely/mock guards and fresh independent review pass. The full real CLI matrix passes 14/14 on this head with PG application anchors intact. Both final-head PG conformance shards are running.

The body records the previous TUI finding's disposition with source and passing boundary tests: TUI/UI loads device identity before transport; the identity-free CLI/BACKEND rule does not apply. No authentication policy or schema was changed.

@clawsweeper re-review

Head: `29a60c022ca97ab3774d83b96c83d55cbb825de3`.

Both remaining owner findings are fixed: the entire updater family retains its own target selection, and engine-selection reads retain the routed environment for subsequent config/state reads. The regressions fail before each correction; 203 focused tests, core types and independent review pass. The final-head PostgreSQL/SQLite CLI matrix passed 14/14, with persisted credentials/config/agent data and anchor-only PostgreSQL application stores. The body records the complete exclusion set and current CI status. Both PostgreSQL conformance shards are running; the prior-head backup timeout remains under investigation.
